=== Nik_2H_1 ===
Seriously Wilhelm, there's no point in trying to weld this many layers, is there? #speaker:Nikki #emotion:annoyed
And c'mon metal, why do you keep cooling so quickly? #speaker:Nikki #emotion:neutral
(She clearly is so focused on her work that she doesn't see you.)

*   [Playfully tease her] 
    Every time you talk to the metal, I'm gonna tell Wilhelm to double the folds. #speaker:*player* #emotion:none #relation_pts:Nikki/3
    (She looks up to pin the voice to the person.) #speaker:none
    Not very smart to threaten a woman holding a hammer, *player*. #speaker:Nikki #emotion:happy
    Point taken. No extra folds. #speaker:*player* #emotion:none
    Now that's more like it. #speaker:Nikki #emotion:happy

*   [Call out her negativity] 
    Do you always complain this much when you have to work? #speaker:*player* #emotion:none #relation_pts:Nikki/-3
    (She looks up, obviously annoyed by the unwelcome comment.) #speaker:none
    No, do you always leer like that at people while they're working? #speaker:Nikki #emotion:annoyed
    Seriously, *player*. I don't go about telling you how to do your work. #emotion:annoyed
    
*   [Stay silent] 
    (Nikki looks up, not expecting to see you in the doorway.) #speaker:none #emotion:none
    Jeez, *player*! Just about gave me a heart attack! #speaker:Nikki #emotion:neutral
    Please tell me you aren't stalking me... #speaker:Nikki #emotion:annoyed
    Because if you are... I'll put you back on the ship and straight into the Sun. #speaker:Nikki #emotion:happy
    Nope, sadly I just got here seconds ago. #speaker:*player* #emotion:none
    
-   Well I'm just about to take a break here -- I'm absolutely exhausted and making zero progress. #speaker:Nikki #emotion:neutral
Meet me outside in a bit, yeah? #speaker:Nikki #emotion:happy
-> END

=== Nik_2H_2 ===
Thanks for waiting, *player*. #speaker:Nikki #emotion:happy
My job on Raea has been, well let's just say, different than I expected. #emotion:neutral
I never expected it to be so labor intensive.
Don't get me wrong, I knew getting a settlement up and running would be insanely tough. #emotion:happy
But I always thought that once we got into our daily routine, we'd have everything we'd need for our jobs. #emotion:sad
You've probably seen by now, but the tech level of my job is pretty medieval. #emotion:neutral
I mean, the settlement has electricity and plumbing. Yet here we are still smelting with blast furnaces. #emotion:annoyed
And just earlier today while on the anvil, I kept stinging my hands whenever I used the hammer wrong.
It's just... I see that you, Jet, and Lucas are more or less working the jobs you trained for. #emotion:sad
And to me, it seems like Jet and Lucas don't even need to work that much. #emotion:happy
Anyways, I know that I should be thankful that we even made it to Raea. #emotion:neutral
But it seems like all those years of training to be an engineer was for nothing. #emotion:sad

*   [Offer a positive spin] 
    Sure, your job wasn't exactly what you thought it was going to be, but look at it this way... #speaker:*player* #emotion:none #relation_pts:Nikki/5
    ...Your training wasn't just work. I'm sure that you met plenty of friends and made some great memories along the way.
    And that alone should make the training worth it, even if the other parts might not be as fruitful.
    Yeah *player*, you got a point. #speaker:Nikki #emotion:happy
    I guess I wouldn't be who I am without those years training with my family at the academy.
    And besides, they would absolutely disappointed if they heard I was complaining about my work on Raea. #emotion:xd
    
*   [Downplay how useful everyone's training was] 
    Ehh... I'm not too sure how useful any of our work will be here on Raea. #speaker:*player* #emotion:none
    I mean... even my work, even though it's still technically botany, is really at this point just simple farming.
    I'm sure anyone on the ship could've done my job.
    And like you said, Lucas and Jet had a wrench thrown in their plans too. Even if they might have some downtime because of it.
    (sigh) Guess you're right. Looks like all our time at our academies might be wasted. #speaker:Nikki #emotion:neutral
    Just makes you think... why we were picked in the first place? #emotion:neutral
    I always thought we were special.
    Maybe we weren't after all... #emotion:sad
    
*   [Be bluntly realistic about work] 
    So it's not your dream job like you thought it was gonna be... #speaker:*player* #emotion:none #relation_pts:Nikki/-3
    I don't see how that's different from what you were told at the academy.
    We were clearly told that this wasn't gonna be all sunshine and rainbows.
    That's clearly not what I meant, and you know it. #speaker:Nikki #emotion:annoyed
    I knew everything was gonna be insanely difficult, and that was IF we ever made it in one piece. 
    I trained and studied endlessly so that I could be helpful in any way I could.
    So when I found out that I was gonna be doing the one thing that I didn't train for, how do you think I felt? #emotion:sad
    It's like a nightmare for me, and I feel useless to the town for having to start from square one.
    
-   Well... thanks for listening to me rant, *player*. #speaker:Nikki #emotion:neutral
I should really be getting back to that anvil.
That iron isn't gonna forge itself after all. #emotion:happy
-> END
